        <ul class="callout-list">
          <li><strong>Widest Price Disparity in US History:</strong> The difference between the cheapest state (<strong>Maine: $1,170/yr</strong>) and the most expensive state (<strong>Florida: $3,640/yr</strong>) exceeds <strong>$2,470 per year</strong> for an identical clean driver profile.</li>
          <li><strong>The No-Fault Penalty:</strong> States with mandatory Personal Injury Protection (PIP) systems (Florida, Michigan, New York) consistently rank among the ten most expensive states due to medical fraud and unlimited treatment provisions.</li>
          <li><strong>Uninsured Motorist Contagion:</strong> In states where more than 20% of drivers are uninsured (such as Mississippi, Michigan, and Tennessee), insured motorists pay an average surcharge of $320/year to subsidize uninsured motorist (UM/UIM) claim pools.</li>
        </ul>
